      "confidence": 0.9,
      "curator_note": "Diethyl ether molecular ion, charge and odd electron localized on oxygen (drawn +•). Book draws 1 arc: a curved full (2-electron) arrow from the C-O sigma bond to O. move <1> is drawn and is the complete electron flow; no implicit move is required because a single 2-electron heterolysis (both C-O bonding electrons to O) fully balances the step, giving C2H5+ (40%) + •OC2H5. In symmetric Et2O either C-O bond is equivalent."
