      "confidence": 0.9,
      "curator_note": "Cross-linked MØD variable: IMS_4_22. MISMATCH - IMS_4_22 DFS '[C]1[C]2[_A+.]3[C]4[C]5>>[C+]1[C]2[_A.]3[C]4[C]5' does NOT cleave any bond (the product is a single connected five-atom chain with no fragment separator), places the + on the terminal methyl (map 1) instead of the carbon that loses the C-O bond, and leaves the heteroatom two-coordinate while marking it a neutral radical (electronically impossible for O). It does not reproduce the drawn C-O inductive heterolysis to C2H5+ + •OC2H5."
